Executive Summary 

 

The Office of Performance and Quality (OPQ) establishes a proactive and structured framework for the adoption and governance of artificial intelligence (AI) within U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS). USCIS has aligned its strategy with federal mandates and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) directives by appointing a Chief AI Officer and forming an AI Governance Board. These governance mechanisms ensure that all AI initiatives advance agency objectives, comply with legal and ethical standards, and incorporate robust risk management practices. 

OPQ leverages DHS Chat as the primary AI tool to streamline code conversion, explanation, optimization, and documentation across technical workflows. By integrating AI capabilities into daily operations, OPQ enhances efficiency, accelerates business processes, and fosters innovation, while maintaining strict human oversight and accountability. OPQ enforces guidelines for generative AI use, prioritizing transparency, explainability, and the protection of privacy and sensitive data. AI applications remain prohibited from performing inherently governmental functions, such as final decision-making in hiring, enforcement, or benefits administration. Comprehensive documentation and records retention requirements apply to all AI-assisted activities, ensuring traceability and compliance. 

OPQ has also identified gaps in existing federal and agency-level guidance, including areas related to implementation, approval, training, and funding. To address these challenges, OPQ has developed USCIS-specific policies and procedures that support responsible and effective AI adoption. Ongoing compliance monitoring, lifecycle management, and workforce training underpin OPQ’s commitment to sustaining operational excellence and responsible innovation. 

OPQ’s approach positions USCIS to leverage AI technologies securely and efficiently, strengthening operational capabilities and reinforcing public trust in the agency’s use of emerging technologies. By maintaining rigorous governance, prioritizing ethical standards, and advancing agency-specific guidance, OPQ provides a strong foundation for expanding AI capabilities and ensuring the responsible integration of AI across USCIS operations. 

 

