Currently Approved Tool(s) 

 

DHS Chat 

 

At the time this document was drafted, DHS Chat is the only AI tool available to the USCIS workforce.  It is well documented at the following URL DHS Chat.  A Rules of Behavior DHS Chat RoB document must be accepted prior to the chat being utilized.  As of this writing, DHS Chat does not incur a cost to components.  However, excessive use may result in the user being blocked from further submissions for a period of time.   

 

Warning 

Information returned via DHS Chat is current only up to a specific date in the past, i.e. DHS is not aware of any events, documents, or information that occurred after its last update.  Part of the condition of DHS being able to utilize an internal LLM is that its not connected the wider internet to preserve guardrails. This results in occasionally outdated knowledge (e.g. it may be unaware of current Executive cabinet members and/or recently released statutes.)  As of this writing DHS Chat is only updated to June 1, 2024 for the Standard model and September 30, 2024 for the Advanced model.   

DHS Chat also cannot reference documents internal to the USCIS Connect, ECN, Sharepoint, Outlook, or TEAMs. It is only able to reference public facing websites. 

 

