The documents referenced above outline requirements for agencies to facilitate the rapid adoption of Artificial Intelligence (AI). Agencies are directed to innovate while delivering value, maximizing transparency, ensuring taxpayer resources are being spent wisely, and focusing on AI products offered by American companies while minimizing risk. This EO rescinds earlier guidance and establishes new requirements for AI leadership, governance, risk management, and interagency coordination. It also prioritizes innovation, governance, and enhancing public trust. 

   

The EO directs agencies to: 

Appoint a Chief AI Officer (CAIO) 

Implement minimum risk management practices for "high-risk AI" 

Provide annual AI use case inventory, compliance plans, and reports 

Establish an AI Governance Board 

Develop Compliance Plans 

Develop an AI Strategy 

Share data and AI assets internally and across agencies to maximize savings and efficiency (Leverage and share AI code and models) 

Use American AI products and services 

Follow effective Federal Procurement processes 

Prepare an AI-Ready workforce through hiring and training 

Achieve AI literacy 

Create an AI Governance program that will accelerate innovation 

Foster public trust in AI by establishing appropriate risk mitigation strategies, delivering high impact use cases, and explaining AI through clear and understandable language 

 

