Documentation 

 

OPQ requires the following documentation for any AI Use Case.  Templates are provided with this document to capture information during the lifecycle of any AI solution. 

Project Plan 

This document will grow as it progresses through the lifecycle of the AI solution.  It should be considered a foundational document for initial approval through disposition.  It will contain information on the justification, process, tools, methodology, and points of contact.  Any waivers to AI policy must be captured in this document. 

AI Model Bias 

This document will outline the evaluation of any bias the AI model is at risk of encountering.  If bias is not a risk for this model, one copy of this document should be created explaining the reasoning.  If bias is a risk, this document will address and findings and their remediation.  If the model is at risk for exhibiting bias based on the types of data included, a copy of this document should be created during each evaluation. 

Model Training 

This document must be created to describe the initial production training process for the model.  A new copy should be created whenever the model is retrained.  This document must capture information on the efficiency and accuracy of the model, paying particular attention to any significant deviations from the initially approved model.  Significant differences may require re-review as part of the governance process. 

Audit 

Periodic auditing is a requirement for all AI models in production.  This document must be generated for each audit to clearly capture the purpose of the audit, and findings from the audit. 

Test Plan 

This document will explain the methods being used to test the model.  It is used for periodic testing to ensure the entire project pipeline is working as expected. 

 

